"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Other","description":"A personal project on object detection and bounding-box location within a driving context.","topics":[],"score":181224,"global_rank":403738},{"name":"dustyjewett/igdb-api-proxy","owner":"dustyjewett","html_url":"https://github.com/dustyjewett/igdb-api-proxy","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Other","description":"A docker image for proxying requests from a client to igdb.","topics":[],"score":181224,"global_rank":403739},{"name":"sfkunal/DataPrivacy_RESEARCH","owner":"sfkunal","html_url":"https://github.com/sfkunal/DataPrivacy_RESEARCH","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Other","description":"The world of technology is changing. It used to be one where users could post on social media, order clothes online, and play mobile games without a care in the world. As time progressed, companies eventually realized that they could collect small pieces of information from a user\u2019s technological habits, and use that to form a profile of the user of some sort. I used a packet-monitoring service to listen in on third-party applications and wrote a script to filter out relevant pieces of data that were being sent back to an application\u2019s server. The findings of this study concluded that third-party iOS applications have unmonitored power to access pieces of information like contacts, location, and emails.","topics":[],"score":181224,"global_rank":403740},{"name":"davidklett/katacoda-scenarios","owner":"davidklett","html_url":"https://github.com/davidklett/katacoda-scenarios","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Other","description":"Katacoda Scenarios","topics":[],"score":181224,"global_rank":403741},{"name":"baumanab/gg","owner":"baumanab","html_url":"https://github.com/baumanab/gg","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Other","description":"gg","topics":[],"score":181224,"global_rank":403742},{"name":"thornrae/reading-note